non-positive by the one-variable second-derivative test. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:differential-vanishes-at-max","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:smooth-local-extension","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:hessian-symmetric","title":"lem:hessian-symmetric","label":"lem:hessian-symmetric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:differential-vanishes-at-max","title":"lem:differential-vanishes-at-max","label":"lem:differential-vanishes-at-max"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:integral-curve-exists","title":"lem:integral-curve-exists","label":"lem:integral-curve-exists"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:second-derivative-test-max","title":"lem:second-derivative-test-max","label":"lem:second-derivative-test-max"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:laplacian-nonpositive-at-max","title":"lem:laplacian-nonpositive-at-max","label":"lem:laplacian-nonpositive-at-max"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:hessian-nonpositive-at-max","title":"lem:hessian-nonpositive-at-max","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[Hessian is negative semi-definite at a local maximum]\n\\label{lem:hessian-nonpositive-at-max}\n\n\\uses{lem:hessian-symmetric}\n\n\n\nFor a smooth function with a local maximum at $q$ and any affine\nconnection,\n$$\\Hess(f)_q(v,v)\\le0\\qquad(v\\in T_qM).$$\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{lem:differential-vanishes-at-max,lem:integral-curve-exists,lem:second-derivative-test-max,lem:hessian-symmetric}\nExtend $v$ to a field $X$ and let $\\gamma$ be its integral curve.\nBecause $df_q=0$,\n$\\Hess(f)_q(v,v)=X(Xf)(q)=(f\\circ\\gamma)''(0)$, which is non-positive\nby the one-variable second-derivative test.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:hessian-symmetric","title":"lem:hessian-symmetric","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:differential-vanishes-at-max","title":"lem:differential-vanishes-at-max","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:integral-curve-exists","title":"lem:integral-curve-exists","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:second-derivative-test-max","title":"lem:second-derivative-test-max","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}